# SAMPLE translation (not core language): PARTIAL DORA Art. 5–6 slice.
# Not a complete mapping of those articles — see README for coverage.
# Working excerpts: ./sources/ — Official Journal / EUR-Lex remain authoritative.
# Lifecycle states (Draft/Approved/…) are a modelling choice for builders, not
# labels from the instrument; for pure standing duties see kind: obligations.

tundra: dora-ict-risk-governance

regulation:
  id: DORA
  instrument: "Regulation (EU) 2022/2554"
  eli: "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2022/2554/oj"
  edition: "OJ L 333, 27.12.2022"
  notes: "Article and paragraph are primary cites. Page omitted until OJ PDF mapping is pinned."

roles:
  - Financial entity
  - Management body
  - Control function
  - Internal audit
  - Competent authority

relationships:
  - Management body is Governing body of Financial entity
  - Control function is Overseer of ICT risk
  - Internal audit is Auditor of ICT risk management framework
  - Competent authority is Supervisor of Financial entity

contracts:
  - id: fe-has-ict-governance-framework
    text: >
      The Financial entity must maintain an internal governance and control
      framework for ICT risk that implements the ICT risk management framework.
    cite:
      - article: "5"
        paragraph: "1"
        quote: "internal governance and control framework that ensures an effective and prudent management of ICT risk"

  - id: mgmt-body-owns-ict-risk-framework
    text: >
      The Management body must define, approve, oversee and be responsible for
      implementing the arrangements of the ICT risk management framework.
    cite:
      - article: "5"
        paragraph: "2"
        quote: "define, approve, oversee and be responsible for the implementation of all arrangements related to the ICT risk management framework"

  - id: mgmt-body-ultimate-ict-risk
    text: >
      The Management body bears ultimate responsibility for managing the
      Financial entity's ICT risk.
    cite:
      - article: "5"
        paragraph: "2(a)"
        quote: "bear the ultimate responsibility for managing the financial entity’s ICT risk"

  - id: mgmt-body-approves-dor-strategy
    text: >
      The Management body must set and approve the digital operational
      resilience strategy, including the ICT risk tolerance level of the
      Financial entity.
    cite:
      - article: "5"
        paragraph: "2(d)"
        quote: "setting and approving the digital operational resilience strategy"

  - id: fe-documented-ict-risk-framework
    text: >
      The Financial entity must have a documented ICT risk management framework
      as part of its overall risk management system.
    cite:
      - article: "6"
        paragraph: "1"
        quote: "sound, comprehensive and well-documented ICT risk management framework as part of their overall risk management system"

  - id: framework-covers-assets-and-premises
    text: >
      The ICT risk management framework must include strategies, policies,
      procedures, ICT protocols and tools that protect information assets and
      ICT assets and the physical components that host them from damage and
      unauthorised access or usage.
    cite:
      - article: "6"
        paragraph: "2"
        quote: "protect all information assets and ICT assets … from risks including damage and unauthorised access or usage"

  - id: control-function-independent-ict-risk
    text: >
      The Financial entity (other than a microenterprise) must assign managing
      and overseeing ICT risk to a Control function that is independent enough
      to avoid conflicts of interest, with segregation among ICT risk management,
      control, and Internal audit (three lines of defence or equivalent).
    cite:
      - article: "6"
        paragraph: "4"
        quote: "assign the responsibility for managing and overseeing ICT risk to a control function"

  - id: framework-review-at-least-yearly
    text: >
      The ICT risk management framework must be documented and reviewed at least
      once every 1 year (or periodically if the Financial entity is a
      microenterprise), and also after major ICT-related incidents and after
      relevant supervisory instructions, digital operational resilience testing,
      or audit conclusions.
    cite:
      - article: "6"
        paragraph: "5"
        quote: "documented and reviewed at least once a year, or periodically in the case of microenterprises"

  - id: framework-review-report-to-authority
    text: >
      When the Competent authority requests it, the Financial entity must submit
      a report on the review of the ICT risk management framework.
    cite:
      - article: "6"
        paragraph: "5"
        quote: "A report on the review of the ICT risk management framework shall be submitted to the competent authority upon its request"

  - id: framework-includes-dor-strategy
    text: >
      The ICT risk management framework must include a digital operational
      resilience strategy that states how the framework is implemented, including
      ICT risk tolerance, information security objectives with KPIs and key risk
      metrics, and mechanisms to detect and protect against ICT-related incidents.
    cite:
      - article: "6"
        paragraph: "8"
        quote: "The ICT risk management framework shall include a digital operational resilience strategy"

  - id: outsourcing-keeps-fe-responsible
    text: >
      If verification of compliance with ICT risk management requirements is
      outsourced, the Financial entity remains fully responsible for that
      verification.
    cite:
      - article: "6"
        paragraph: "10"
        quote: "the financial entity remains fully responsible for the verification of compliance with the ICT risk management requirements"

states:
  - ICT risk management framework is Draft
  - ICT risk management framework is Approved
  - name: ICT risk management framework is Under review
  - name: ICT risk management framework is Current
    final: true

processes:
  - name: Draft ICT risk management framework
    actor: Financial entity
    requires: no ICT risk management framework exists
    results: ICT risk management framework is Draft
    enforced_by:
      - fe-documented-ict-risk-framework
      - framework-covers-assets-and-premises
      - framework-includes-dor-strategy
    cite:
      - article: "6"
        paragraph: "1"

  - name: Approve ICT risk management framework
    actor: Management body
    requires: ICT risk management framework is Draft
    results: ICT risk management framework is Approved
    enforced_by:
      - mgmt-body-owns-ict-risk-framework
      - mgmt-body-ultimate-ict-risk
      - mgmt-body-approves-dor-strategy
      - fe-has-ict-governance-framework
    cite:
      - article: "5"
        paragraph: "2"

  - name: Assign ICT risk control function
    actor: Financial entity
    requires: ICT risk management framework is Approved
    results: ICT risk management framework is Current
    enforced_by:
      - control-function-independent-ict-risk
    cite:
      - article: "6"
        paragraph: "4"

  - name: Review ICT risk management framework
    actor: Management body
    requires: ICT risk management framework is Current
    results: ICT risk management framework is Under review
    enforced_by:
      - framework-review-at-least-yearly
    cite:
      - article: "6"
        paragraph: "5"

  - name: Complete framework review
    actor: Management body
    requires: ICT risk management framework is Under review
    results: ICT risk management framework is Current
    enforced_by:
      - framework-review-at-least-yearly
      - framework-review-report-to-authority
    cite:
      - article: "6"
        paragraph: "5"

scenarios:
  - name: "Happy path: framework drafted, approved, control assigned, kept current"
    steps:
      - Given no ICT risk management framework exists
      - When the Financial entity drafts the ICT risk management framework
      - Then the ICT risk management framework is Draft
      - When the Management body approves the ICT risk management framework
      - Then the ICT risk management framework is Approved
      - When the Financial entity assigns the ICT risk Control function
      - Then the ICT risk management framework is Current

  - name: "Error: approve without management body ownership"
    steps:
      - Given the ICT risk management framework is Draft
      - When a party other than the Management body tries to approve the ICT risk management framework
      - Then the approval is rejected
      - And the contract [mgmt-body-owns-ict-risk-framework] is broken

  - name: "Error: outsource verification and drop accountability"
    steps:
      - Given the ICT risk management framework is Current
      - When the Financial entity outsources verification of ICT risk management compliance and treats itself as not responsible
      - Then the arrangement is non-compliant
      - And the contract [outsourcing-keeps-fe-responsible] is broken
